WEBVTT

00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:30.791
and we mapped their hunting behavior

00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:32.239
from the air.

00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:34.905
The lower left shows a lion sizing up

00:00:34.905 --> 00:00:36.917
a herd of impala for a kill,

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:38.486
and the right shows what I call

00:00:38.486 --> 00:00:40.349
the lion viewshed.

00:00:40.349 --> 00:00:42.971
That's how far the lion can see in all directions

00:00:42.971 --> 00:00:47.146
until his or her view is obstructed by vegetation.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.587
And what we found

00:00:48.587 --> 00:00:51.093
is that male lions are not the lazy hunters

00:00:51.093 --> 00:00:52.617
we thought them to be.

00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:54.754
They just use a different strategy.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.506
Whereas the female lions hunt

00:00:56.506 --> 00:00:57.638
out in the open savanna

00:00:57.638 --> 00:01:00.299
over long distances, usually during the day,